1
00:00:00,006 --> 00:00:01,427
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,448 --> 00:00:03,007
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,362 --> 00:00:04,636
The woman I'm seeing...

4
00:00:05,691 --> 00:00:07,497
is Ji Ni's father's official wife.

5
00:00:08,462 --> 00:00:11,543
The one who wouldn't agree to a divorce,
making Ji Ni suffer as a child.

6
00:00:12,027 --> 00:00:13,135
What?

7
00:00:15,173 --> 00:00:16,490
How is that possible?

8
00:00:17,295 --> 00:00:20,339
- But you said she was widowed.
- The thing is...

9
00:00:20,718 --> 00:00:22,580
That was ages ago for her...

10
00:00:23,009 --> 00:00:26,267
Anyway, please stop Do Hee from talking.

11
00:00:26,342 --> 00:00:27,927
I think Do Hee called Ji Ni...

12
00:00:28,166 --> 00:00:30,612
the daughter of a mistress,

13
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:32,634
and I don't want her saying anything else.

14
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:34,078
That's the favor I came to ask.

15
00:00:35,135 --> 00:00:36,386
Okay.

16
00:00:37,641 --> 00:00:39,590
I'm honestly confused too.

17
00:00:39,653 --> 00:00:43,648
Imagine how I feel.
I haven't even told Joong Bin yet.

18
00:00:43,728 --> 00:00:46,985
If her connection to Ji Ni
becomes known...

19
00:00:49,386 --> 00:00:50,967
Yes. I understand.

20
00:00:52,596 --> 00:00:53,707
Okay.

21
00:00:54,171 --> 00:00:55,171
Joong Bin...

22
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:59,064
- Your father may fire Ji Ni.
- Does that make any sense?

23
00:00:59,387 --> 00:01:01,383
Why should she be fired
over her parents' actions?

24
00:01:01,421 --> 00:01:03,105
That's how our society works.

25
00:01:03,842 --> 00:01:06,906
It's fine as long as no one knows,
but once they do, it becomes a problem.

26
00:01:19,046 --> 00:01:20,321
You scared me!

27
00:01:20,975 --> 00:01:22,015
Joong Bin.

28
00:01:22,343 --> 00:01:24,512
That reaction tells me
you must be hiding something.

29
00:01:24,625 --> 00:01:26,160
What?

30
00:01:26,208 --> 00:01:29,181
I heard that musician is Ji Ni's mother.

31
00:01:30,009 --> 00:01:31,350
Did your wife tell you that?

32
00:01:31,421 --> 00:01:33,072
It doesn't matter who told me.
Just state the facts.

33
00:01:33,409 --> 00:01:35,509
You went to the beach with her, right?

34
00:01:35,582 --> 00:01:37,742
I heard she was a married man's mistress
until he passed away.

35
00:01:37,745 --> 00:01:40,330
What's your point?

36
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:41,921
Why are you raising your voice?

37
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:45,949
Because you're interrogating me
first thing in the morning.

38
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,703
You little...

39
00:01:48,122 --> 00:01:49,927
I really want you to get married, but...

40
00:01:49,948 --> 00:01:52,491
not to a former mistress
who's now a widow. Got it?

41
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:55,425
That's not our relationship. We're...

42
00:01:55,796 --> 00:01:58,344
only meeting as fellow human beings.

43
00:01:58,402 --> 00:01:59,476
Is that true?

44
00:02:00,182 --> 00:02:02,642
Then keep it that way.

45
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:04,516
Anything more is out of the question.

46
00:02:05,497 --> 00:02:08,259
- Why shouldn't it?
- What did you say?

47
00:02:08,407 --> 00:02:12,344
Even former convicts are given
a second chance in society.

48
00:02:13,682 --> 00:02:15,969
As they should be. So why...

49
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:19,136
judge someone because of their past...

50
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:22,082
What? Were you seeing her
while claiming she was just a musician?

51
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:24,659
Were you waiting for her husband to die?
That makes you her affair partner!

52
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:26,625
A homewrecker...

53
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:31,097
How could you even imagine that?
That's ridiculous.

54
00:02:31,181 --> 00:02:33,603
If I'm wrong, fine.
Just date someone normal, okay?

55
00:02:33,707 --> 00:02:36,528
A woman who can have children with you
and build a family together.

56
00:02:37,382 --> 00:02:40,359
How am I supposed to have a child?

57
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:43,395
Even if I did, I'd be 70
by the time they reached college.

58
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,423
When they start kindergarten,
I'll send Ji Hu in my place.

59
00:02:50,912 --> 00:02:53,713
Don't laugh. This is reality.

60
00:03:09,345 --> 00:03:11,058
- Is it done?
- Yes, sir.

61
00:03:13,552 --> 00:03:14,610
Lieutenant No,

62
00:03:15,478 --> 00:03:17,737
what did you think of Na Ji Ni
from our publishing house?

63
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,490
I had a good impression of her.

64
00:03:20,582 --> 00:03:23,164
Judging children
for their parents' mistakes...

65
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:24,554
is rather old-fashioned, right?

66
00:03:24,566 --> 00:03:27,800
- That depends on the mistake.
- Give an example.

67
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:32,848
I can forgive anything but cheating.

68
00:03:33,811 --> 00:03:36,633
- That's just my own opinion.
- Cheating.

69
00:03:37,493 --> 00:03:38,509
Right.

70
00:03:39,893 --> 00:03:42,648
You once left your unit without permission
because your sister was cheated on, right?

71
00:03:42,752 --> 00:03:43,752
Yes, sir.

72
00:03:43,990 --> 00:03:45,434
I was going to kill him, but...

73
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:47,711
you stopped me in time, sir.

74
00:03:48,048 --> 00:03:49,854
I'll always be grateful to you.

75
00:03:50,486 --> 00:03:52,067
How is your sister doing now?

76
00:03:52,444 --> 00:03:55,077
- She's doing well, raising her children.
- And your brother-in-law?

77
00:03:55,682 --> 00:03:57,602
He croaked from an illness not long ago.

78
00:03:58,326 --> 00:03:59,519
He got what he deserved.

79
00:04:00,086 --> 00:04:02,735
He was never a brother-in-law to me.

80
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,188
Let's go.

81
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:13,981
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

82
00:04:17,493 --> 00:04:21,408
It looks like he went into septic shock.
You must've been frightened.

83
00:04:21,463 --> 00:04:23,720
Why did it happen?

84
00:04:24,819 --> 00:04:27,608
I did everything exactly as you told me.

85
00:04:27,611 --> 00:04:30,200
This wasn't caused by carelessness.

86
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,208
You both handled everything perfectly.

87
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:37,042
But O Reum can become seriously ill
from even a minor infection.

88
00:04:37,442 --> 00:04:39,344
He woke up briefly last night, but...

89
00:04:40,305 --> 00:04:42,367
he seems unconscious again now.

90
00:04:43,548 --> 00:04:46,235
So what should we do?
Does he need to be hospitalized again?

91
00:04:47,918 --> 00:04:50,851
We need to keep him
under close observation for now.

92
00:04:51,206 --> 00:04:52,206
Well, then.

93
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,740
Mom, go home.

94
00:05:05,084 --> 00:05:08,160
Okay. I'll make some food
and bring it over.

95
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,642
I don't want to eat.

96
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,971
How can I eat at a time like this?

97
00:05:31,695 --> 00:05:34,019
Did you prepare all of this?

98
00:05:35,796 --> 00:05:37,131
It's nothing.

99
00:05:37,202 --> 00:05:40,149
I just packed some rice
with the side dishes we had.

100
00:05:40,604 --> 00:05:41,796
Look at all this.

101
00:05:43,742 --> 00:05:48,085
I wanted to write something encouraging,
but I'm not very good with words,

102
00:05:48,427 --> 00:05:49,695
so I drew this instead.

103
00:05:58,742 --> 00:06:01,262
Thank you. I'll make sure they get it.

104
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,596
It'll mean a lot to them.

105
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:07,552
- I have to go to work now.
- Okay.

106
00:06:24,992 --> 00:06:27,765
Yes. Did you check at the station?

107
00:06:29,636 --> 00:06:30,795
There was nothing, right?

108
00:06:32,545 --> 00:06:36,314
You handled it well. Thank you.

109
00:06:41,545 --> 00:06:44,602
- Nothing at all?
- I just checked at the police station.

110
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:47,040
Nothing. No one looked like Do Hee.

111
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,760
See? I told you it wasn't her.

112
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,581
You were too quick to suspect her
because of that high school incident.

113
00:06:52,992 --> 00:06:55,591
- I can't believe it.
- Anyway, I came to let you know.

114
00:06:56,096 --> 00:06:57,375
I should get to work.

115
00:06:57,997 --> 00:06:58,997
Okay.

116
00:07:01,598 --> 00:07:04,857
No way. I was so sure.

117
00:07:05,728 --> 00:07:08,136
I'm relieved. I'm sorry I suspected you.

118
00:07:12,218 --> 00:07:13,360
Do Hee.

119
00:07:13,594 --> 00:07:17,120
Even if everyone says I did it,
shouldn't you be on my side?

120
00:07:18,474 --> 00:07:20,590
I'm really disappointed in you.

121
00:07:21,282 --> 00:07:22,550
I'm truly sorry.

122
00:07:23,404 --> 00:07:25,981
More than anyone, I wanted to believe
you were innocent.

123
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:28,432
I know. That's why I'm forgiving you.

124
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:32,929
I'll never doubt you again.

125
00:07:40,497 --> 00:07:41,541
Apologize.

126
00:07:42,970 --> 00:07:46,076
- Do Hee.
- You should apologize too.

127
00:07:47,168 --> 00:07:50,768
You even made my fiancé, Ji Hu,
suspect me.

128
00:07:51,568 --> 00:07:53,340
Do you know how humiliated I felt?

129
00:07:53,695 --> 00:07:56,848
Okay. I'm sorry. It was my fault.

130
00:07:57,737 --> 00:07:59,813
No. I should be the one to apologize.

131
00:08:00,352 --> 00:08:03,552
He only sided with me
because I suspected you first.

132
00:08:04,478 --> 00:08:06,799
- I was wrong.
- I told you...

133
00:08:07,505 --> 00:08:08,966
I've changed.

134
00:08:09,592 --> 00:08:12,116
Why don't you believe me?
Why do you doubt me?

135
00:08:12,932 --> 00:08:14,715
Isn't that a baseless accusation?

136
00:08:15,265 --> 00:08:17,477
You're right. I was careless.

137
00:08:18,659 --> 00:08:19,796
I'm sorry.

138
00:08:20,522 --> 00:08:23,224
You should get on your knees
and apologize properly.

139
00:08:23,682 --> 00:08:26,493
Otherwise, I'll sue you for defamation
and seek damages.

140
00:08:28,086 --> 00:08:29,976
Get on your knees!

141
00:08:30,162 --> 00:08:32,469
If you're going to apologize,
do it properly. Okay?

142
00:08:34,326 --> 00:08:36,554
Fine. Then you apologize too.

143
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:39,577
- What?
- You have nothing to apologize to me for?

144
00:08:39,977 --> 00:08:42,747
No. You're the mistress's daughter.

145
00:08:42,870 --> 00:08:44,095
Is that a lie?

146
00:08:44,462 --> 00:08:45,927
So what do I have to apologize for?

147
00:08:47,754 --> 00:08:48,971
Enough.

148
00:08:50,958 --> 00:08:52,647
I understand that you feel wronged,

149
00:08:53,067 --> 00:08:56,340
but you're both still young.
Dragging your parents' private matters...

150
00:08:56,365 --> 00:08:57,727
into this doesn't look good.

151
00:08:57,808 --> 00:08:59,173
Father.

152
00:09:00,411 --> 00:09:04,904
This is so unfair. She called me a thief.

153
00:09:05,017 --> 00:09:08,890
I've never been falsely accused
of something so outrageous in my life.

154
00:09:09,991 --> 00:09:11,216
I'm sorry.

155
00:09:11,582 --> 00:09:13,832
We were thoughtless.

156
00:09:15,282 --> 00:09:16,390
I'm sorry too.

157
00:09:16,442 --> 00:09:17,822
Yes, you were in the wrong.

158
00:09:17,876 --> 00:09:20,583
- Calling her a thief without evidence.
- Yes.

159
00:09:21,177 --> 00:09:23,266
I'll let it go for your sake, Father.

160
00:09:23,615 --> 00:09:25,364
We're also classmates.

161
00:09:25,931 --> 00:09:28,781
- I don't want to be too harsh on her.
- Good.

162
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:31,500
You're very understanding.
Now, go outside.

163
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,800
I care about you,

164
00:09:38,861 --> 00:09:41,677
but I even asked you to be careful.
Do Hee's my future daughter-in-law.

165
00:09:41,698 --> 00:09:42,760
How could you casually call her a thief?

166
00:09:44,238 --> 00:09:45,719
I was careless.

167
00:09:46,061 --> 00:09:49,844
If she marries Ji Hu, I plan to put her
in charge of this publishing company too.

168
00:09:50,011 --> 00:09:52,271
- Father.
- Not right away, of course,

169
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,299
but I won't be working forever, right?

170
00:09:56,074 --> 00:09:59,129
Ji Ni, focus more
on organizing the archives.

171
00:10:00,356 --> 00:10:01,356
Yes.

172
00:10:02,566 --> 00:10:03,796
Understood.

173
00:10:19,084 --> 00:10:20,469
Thank you.

174
00:10:21,691 --> 00:10:22,975
Thank you.

175
00:10:40,907 --> 00:10:42,338
So this is where you were.

176
00:10:43,876 --> 00:10:45,791
I'm sorry. This happened because of me.

177
00:10:47,657 --> 00:10:50,100
It's okay. I was suspicious too.

178
00:10:51,795 --> 00:10:56,340
If Do Do Hee didn't take the tablet,
then who did?

179
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:59,531
- And why would they take it?
- Forget about it.

180
00:10:59,682 --> 00:11:01,885
We restored all the paintings anyway.

181
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:04,550
There was something more important on it.

182
00:11:06,722 --> 00:11:08,969
My bone marrow donation certificate,

183
00:11:09,451 --> 00:11:10,832
my mom's will,

184
00:11:11,594 --> 00:11:12,907
and my paintings of my dad.

185
00:11:14,272 --> 00:11:16,751
They're things money can't buy.

186
00:11:17,162 --> 00:11:18,552
That's what hurts the most.

187
00:11:20,217 --> 00:11:22,001
I see. I didn't know.

188
00:11:23,505 --> 00:11:27,345
- So that's what was in the tablet case.
- Yes.

189
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,413
They're important to me,

190
00:11:30,842 --> 00:11:33,101
but they're useless to whoever took them.

191
00:11:33,662 --> 00:11:35,427
They'll probably just throw them away.

192
00:11:36,235 --> 00:11:38,321
I just hope they give them back.

193
00:11:39,568 --> 00:11:42,975
I really regret leaving the tablet
there that day.

194
00:11:43,118 --> 00:11:47,732
With everything going on with O Reum,
I can't even tell you to cheer up.

195
00:11:56,543 --> 00:11:58,332
Look at you eating, O Reum.

196
00:11:58,335 --> 00:12:01,147
- I'll grow up to be as tall as you, Dad.
- Really?

197
00:12:01,499 --> 00:12:04,720
I'll drive a car, just like you.

198
00:12:05,291 --> 00:12:06,979
Wouldn't that be cool?

199
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:09,724
- Who will you take for a ride?
- Mom and grandma.

200
00:12:10,078 --> 00:12:13,404
- What about me?
- You already have your own car.

201
00:12:13,813 --> 00:12:16,739
You should take me for a ride too.

202
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,823
Your hair has gotten so long.

203
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:27,150
- I'm done eating.
- Want me to hold you until you sleep?

204
00:12:31,265 --> 00:12:32,731
My boy.

205
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:34,870
Want me to get you some coffee?

206
00:12:35,973 --> 00:12:40,053
- You can't have that. What do you want?
- Something sweet. Anything.

207
00:13:05,936 --> 00:13:08,630
Hello. What brings you here?

208
00:13:10,151 --> 00:13:11,895
I came for the singing class,
but they said it was canceled.

209
00:13:13,295 --> 00:13:14,578
Sa Bin.

210
00:13:17,102 --> 00:13:18,293
Yeong Ju.

211
00:13:19,055 --> 00:13:20,445
You came all the way here...

212
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:26,697
I thought this would be good
for your wife, so I brought it.

213
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,272
I heard she's expecting.

214
00:13:30,107 --> 00:13:32,114
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

215
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:37,278
I told him
you're expecting your second child.

216
00:13:41,402 --> 00:13:44,088
- Let's step outside for a minute.
- Okay.

217
00:14:05,539 --> 00:14:08,411
I called you, but you didn't answer.

218
00:14:09,165 --> 00:14:11,496
I was so worried,
I couldn't just sit around.

219
00:14:11,792 --> 00:14:13,973
I left my phone at home.

220
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,329
I didn't have anyone I needed to call.

221
00:14:17,505 --> 00:14:19,661
Did you call me a lot?

222
00:14:19,922 --> 00:14:22,493
I've never called anyone
this many times before.

223
00:14:23,665 --> 00:14:24,817
Sa Bin.

224
00:14:26,046 --> 00:14:27,849
I just wanted to see your face,

225
00:14:28,448 --> 00:14:31,542
make sure you had something to eat,
and then leave. That's all.

226
00:14:32,823 --> 00:14:34,164
Thank you.

227
00:14:35,885 --> 00:14:37,082
Now that I've seen you,

228
00:14:37,281 --> 00:14:38,453
I'll get going.

229
00:14:40,698 --> 00:14:42,978
No one's ever worried about me...

230
00:14:43,990 --> 00:14:45,283
like this before.

231
00:14:46,656 --> 00:14:48,365
Thank you for understanding.

232
00:14:49,366 --> 00:14:51,534
I hope you don't wear yourself out.

233
00:14:52,490 --> 00:14:54,306
Being a grandmother, a mother,
and a mother-in-law...

234
00:14:54,573 --> 00:14:56,906
isn't all you are, Yeong Ju.

235
00:14:57,198 --> 00:14:59,134
You're someone precious to me too.

236
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,240
Mom?

237
00:15:09,226 --> 00:15:10,844
Are you here?

238
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:22,779
Are you here?

239
00:15:23,781 --> 00:15:25,274
You must be worried.

240
00:15:26,127 --> 00:15:28,255
I'll pray that O Reum gets better soon.

241
00:15:28,990 --> 00:15:30,131
Thank you.

242
00:15:32,490 --> 00:15:33,648
You should get going.

243
00:15:34,073 --> 00:15:35,172
Okay.

244
00:15:52,237 --> 00:15:55,238
It's a good thing if someone likes mother.

245
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,240
What's wrong?

246
00:15:56,615 --> 00:15:58,747
Why'd he come all the way here to visit?

247
00:15:58,749 --> 00:15:59,988
Are they family or what?

248
00:15:59,990 --> 00:16:02,056
If he's taking singing lessons,
he should just stick to singing.

249
00:16:02,422 --> 00:16:03,865
And I hear he's tone-deaf too.

250
00:16:05,378 --> 00:16:08,238
What's a tone-deaf person
doing taking singing lessons?

251
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,531
You're the strange one.

252
00:16:10,656 --> 00:16:12,821
You're more like a husband than a son,

253
00:16:12,823 --> 00:16:14,698
but you're not actually her husband.

254
00:16:14,701 --> 00:16:15,771
Who said I was?

255
00:16:24,198 --> 00:16:25,865
How's O Reum?

256
00:16:25,990 --> 00:16:28,475
He was playing until just now,
then he fell asleep.

257
00:16:29,781 --> 00:16:32,258
He's doing much better. That's a relief.

258
00:16:33,221 --> 00:16:34,988
He was laughing earlier,

259
00:16:34,990 --> 00:16:38,198
saying he'd grow as tall as his dad
and drive a car like him.

260
00:16:38,490 --> 00:16:42,538
Thanks so much for the lunchbox
and the drawing.

261
00:16:42,573 --> 00:16:44,488
It was nothing.

262
00:16:44,490 --> 00:16:47,252
It was really good.
We all looked at it for a while.

263
00:16:48,387 --> 00:16:49,652
Thank you.

264
00:16:53,473 --> 00:16:56,320
There's a great place near the office,
so I picked some up.

265
00:16:56,615 --> 00:16:58,185
You need to make sure
you're eating properly.

266
00:16:59,365 --> 00:17:02,513
Dumplings. Thanks. I'll enjoy them.

267
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,240
Sure.

268
00:17:30,892 --> 00:17:32,673
You're late.

269
00:17:32,740 --> 00:17:34,196
Did Joong Bin drink?

270
00:17:34,198 --> 00:17:35,863
Yeah. He had a little.

271
00:17:35,865 --> 00:17:38,000
- I'm leaving then.
- Wait.

272
00:17:38,865 --> 00:17:39,865
Hold on.

273
00:17:41,406 --> 00:17:42,778
Really?

274
00:17:43,316 --> 00:17:46,446
Women often say the opposite
of what they mean.

275
00:17:46,448 --> 00:17:47,669
You have to read between the lines.

276
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:50,238
Of course, women these days
aren't like that,

277
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,615
but older women,

278
00:17:53,251 --> 00:17:54,771
they always mean the exact opposite.

279
00:17:55,281 --> 00:17:57,571
One hundred percent. Right?

280
00:17:58,380 --> 00:17:59,955
She does like me, right?

281
00:18:01,101 --> 00:18:03,997
- Is this your first relationship?
- What? No, it's not...

282
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:07,196
I'm usually busy working
as a doctor of Korean medicine,

283
00:18:07,198 --> 00:18:09,363
and I spend my vacations traveling.

284
00:18:09,365 --> 00:18:11,031
So it's your first.

285
00:18:11,041 --> 00:18:12,960
Then trust your gut,

286
00:18:13,615 --> 00:18:14,738
and charge ahead.

287
00:18:14,740 --> 00:18:18,240
- No retreat, no surrender.
- "Gut?" You mean a feeling?

288
00:18:20,615 --> 00:18:23,634
With a man like you,
she should welcome you with open arms.

289
00:18:23,865 --> 00:18:26,448
What a foolish woman.

290
00:18:27,656 --> 00:18:29,776
That's a bit harsh.

291
00:18:31,865 --> 00:18:32,976
You should stop drinking.

292
00:18:36,209 --> 00:18:40,448
Earlier, when the General was drinking,
I wanted one so badly, but I held back.

293
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:45,365
- I'm sorry.
- No, it's okay. Thanks for the advice.

294
00:18:46,986 --> 00:18:48,988
But it's still a secret for now.

295
00:18:48,990 --> 00:18:50,046
Of course.

296
00:18:50,079 --> 00:18:52,757
I'll keep my lips sealed
until you announce it yourself.

297
00:18:53,957 --> 00:18:54,995
Zip.

298
00:18:55,365 --> 00:18:57,416
Well, I'll get going, Doctor.

299
00:18:57,990 --> 00:18:59,397
I'll take this too.

300
00:19:21,823 --> 00:19:25,394
Where am I, and who am I?

301
00:19:38,107 --> 00:19:42,364
My life sure has taken a strange turn.

302
00:19:57,781 --> 00:19:59,979
Hey, I'm going back.

303
00:20:00,427 --> 00:20:01,988
This isn't really my scene.

304
00:20:01,990 --> 00:20:03,865
It's okay. She likes parties anyway.

305
00:20:06,406 --> 00:20:09,573
Ta-da! What's this?

306
00:20:09,663 --> 00:20:10,825
You came too, Tae O?

307
00:20:10,990 --> 00:20:14,781
Yeah. Ji Hu told me
to come apologize properly.

308
00:20:14,990 --> 00:20:19,404
But I don't think this is the right place
for me. I'll get going.

309
00:20:19,406 --> 00:20:22,823
Hey, you're already here. Stay a while.
It's fine, right?

310
00:20:22,927 --> 00:20:24,260
It'll be awkward with just the two of us.

311
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:27,225
What do you think?

312
00:20:27,613 --> 00:20:29,238
I'm already amazed.

313
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,366
It's beautiful.

314
00:20:30,698 --> 00:20:32,852
Congratulations, Ji Hu.

315
00:20:33,990 --> 00:20:36,225
Hey, I need to use the bathroom.

316
00:20:40,323 --> 00:20:42,448
Why'd he come all the way here?
Can't he take a hint?

317
00:20:42,490 --> 00:20:43,809
I told you, I brought him.

318
00:20:44,858 --> 00:20:45,895
Have a seat, Ji Hu.

319
00:20:53,990 --> 00:20:56,349
I'm sorry. Please forgive Tae O too.

320
00:20:58,495 --> 00:21:00,677
Don't ever doubt me again.

321
00:21:06,115 --> 00:21:07,115
Cheers.

322
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:09,740
Let's drink arm-in-arm.

323
00:21:15,406 --> 00:21:18,300
Singles pour their own drinks.

324
00:21:19,531 --> 00:21:21,488
- Aren't you hungry?
- Yeah.

325
00:21:21,490 --> 00:21:23,276
Take your time and enjoy the food.

326
00:21:24,031 --> 00:21:25,486
Can I look around the house?

327
00:21:27,067 --> 00:21:28,740
This place is amazing.

328
00:21:28,903 --> 00:21:30,594
Go ahead. It's nothing special.

329
00:21:31,115 --> 00:21:32,696
You should move out too.
What's stopping you?

330
00:21:32,698 --> 00:21:34,721
My dad's the problem.

331
00:21:36,073 --> 00:21:38,424
Okay, let's take a look around.

332
00:21:48,588 --> 00:21:50,346
It's been so long
since you've smiled like this.

333
00:21:52,281 --> 00:21:54,460
- Ji Hu, let's dance.
- What?

334
00:21:57,698 --> 00:21:59,225
He said he was going to look around.

335
00:21:59,490 --> 00:22:01,349
Tae O gave us some privacy.

336
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:09,157
- It's been forever.
- I know.

337
00:22:27,198 --> 00:22:29,113
Not a single one is finished.

338
00:22:29,115 --> 00:22:31,017
A budding celebrity, indeed.

339
00:22:40,948 --> 00:22:42,024
It's all over me.

340
00:22:44,781 --> 00:22:46,656
(Stem Cell Donation Certificate, Na Ji Ni)

341
00:23:12,115 --> 00:23:13,695
Tae O, what are you doing? Come out.

342
00:23:14,323 --> 00:23:15,733
Yeah.

343
00:23:24,281 --> 00:23:27,616
Hey, you were dancing,
and now you're eating?

344
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:30,732
Don't be jealous. Hurry up
and get yourself a girlfriend.

345
00:23:30,948 --> 00:23:32,281
Hey, you're pretty cheesy too.

346
00:23:32,296 --> 00:23:33,296
When did you learn to dance?

347
00:23:33,323 --> 00:23:35,071
Cheesy, right? I thought so at first too.

348
00:23:35,073 --> 00:23:37,222
People in England all dance at parties.

349
00:23:37,281 --> 00:23:38,691
If you don't, it's embarrassing.

350
00:23:39,990 --> 00:23:41,823
We thought it was super cheesy
at first too.

351
00:23:41,855 --> 00:23:42,855
Yeah.

352
00:23:43,573 --> 00:23:46,238
I couldn't dance at first,
so I felt awkward,

353
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:47,988
and I left early by myself to go home.

354
00:23:47,990 --> 00:23:49,562
Then I got mugged by some thugs,

355
00:23:49,905 --> 00:23:52,686
and that's when I met Ji Hu.
My Prince Charming.

356
00:23:52,906 --> 00:23:54,240
That's when our story began.

357
00:23:55,299 --> 00:23:56,727
That's quite a story.

358
00:23:58,217 --> 00:24:00,903
- Cheers.
- What? You're letting me join?

359
00:24:01,957 --> 00:24:02,957
Okay.

360
00:24:04,156 --> 00:24:05,623
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

361
00:24:12,077 --> 00:24:13,410
- It's delicious.
- Right?

362
00:24:22,406 --> 00:24:24,678
If O Reum doesn't recover,

363
00:24:24,855 --> 00:24:26,602
we'll have to leave here, right?

364
00:24:27,490 --> 00:24:29,446
We can only stay here...

365
00:24:29,448 --> 00:24:31,238
if that kid keeps smiling.

366
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:33,740
Mom, how can you say that right now?

367
00:24:33,781 --> 00:24:36,156
He's not the only one fighting
for his life.

368
00:24:36,222 --> 00:24:38,462
I'm barely getting by myself.

369
00:24:39,906 --> 00:24:42,770
I sold everything and came here
because I couldn't afford the interest.

370
00:24:46,281 --> 00:24:47,490
What's wrong with you?

371
00:25:12,049 --> 00:25:13,592
O Reum.

372
00:25:14,615 --> 00:25:16,279
O Reum, what's wrong?

373
00:25:16,281 --> 00:25:18,195
O Reum.

374
00:25:19,365 --> 00:25:21,156
What should I do?

375
00:25:25,490 --> 00:25:28,406
- Mom.
- Yes.

376
00:25:50,694 --> 00:25:51,915
O Reum.

377
00:25:53,781 --> 00:25:56,325
O Reum.

378
00:25:56,656 --> 00:25:58,156
O Reum.

379
00:25:58,490 --> 00:26:00,198
O Reum.

380
00:26:01,698 --> 00:26:03,490
O Reum.

381
00:26:04,031 --> 00:26:05,461
O Reum.

382
00:26:08,031 --> 00:26:09,656
What's wrong with him? O Reum.

383
00:26:11,948 --> 00:26:14,365
O Reum.

384
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:36,240
No.

385
00:27:51,031 --> 00:27:53,365
- O Reum.
- No...

386
00:28:27,615 --> 00:28:30,863
(Family Register)

387
00:28:30,870 --> 00:28:32,118
It's all because of you.

388
00:28:32,121 --> 00:28:33,787
All you care about is dating.

389
00:28:33,823 --> 00:28:35,988
If we'd gotten the bone marrow
when he was stronger...

390
00:28:35,990 --> 00:28:38,115
You kept making people come and beg you.

391
00:28:38,198 --> 00:28:39,531
Didn't you make quite a show of it?

392
00:28:39,573 --> 00:28:41,863
What else could I do?
I'm just being realistic.

393
00:28:41,865 --> 00:28:44,446
- I'm the person who called ahead.
- The part-time worker?

394
00:28:44,448 --> 00:28:46,196
- What kind of part-time job?
- It's a secret.

395
00:28:46,198 --> 00:28:48,363
- Love in Zip.
- How childish.

396
00:28:48,365 --> 00:28:50,696
Classy doesn't work.
Childish is the theme.

397
00:28:50,698 --> 00:28:53,446
Her name is Do Do Hee. From the photos,
she looks like she comes from money.

398
00:28:53,448 --> 00:28:54,696
Are you in love with Do Hee?

399
00:28:54,698 --> 00:28:56,198
Why are you suddenly asking that?

400
00:28:57,429 --> 00:28:59,429
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
